📁 Output Files
File	Description
product_prices.csv	Spreadsheet with converted prices
product_prices.json	JSON format data
price_comparison_chart.png	Bar chart visualization
🛠 Tech Stack
Python 3.7+

Requests + BeautifulSoup (scraping)

Pandas (tables)

Matplotlib (charts)

ExchangeRate-API (free, no key)

📂 Project Structure
text
project/
├── pricescraper.py          # Main script
├── requirements.txt         # Dependencies
├── README.md               # This file
├── screenshots/            # Screenshot folder
│   ├── 1-menu.png
│   ├── 2-results.png
│   └── 3-chart.png
└── output/                 # Generated files
    ├── product_prices.csv
    ├── product_prices.json
    └── price_comparison_chart.png
🔧 Troubleshooting
Issue	Fix
ModuleNotFoundError	Run pip install -r requirements.txt
AttributeError: 'run'	Check method indentation in class
Connection error	Check internet connection
📝 requirements.txt
txt
requests>=2.31.0
beautifulsoup4>=4.12.0
pandas>=2.0.0
matplotlib>=3.7.0
🎯 Usage Example
python
from pricescraper import PriceScraperCurrencyConverter

scraper = PriceScraperCurrencyConverter()
scraper.run(target_currency="KES", num_products=10)
📸 Taking Screenshots
Create screenshots folder:

bash
mkdir screenshots
Run script and capture:

Menu screen: When currency options appear → save as screenshots/1-menu.png

Results table: After scraping completes → save as screenshots/2-results.png

Chart: When matplotlib window opens → save as screenshots/3-chart.png

✅ Run Commands
bash
# Setup
python -m venv venv
source venv/Scripts/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Run
python pricescraper.py

# Deactivate
deactivate
